(vector (map (:registry/operating-states (vector :intake :propose :approve :execute :audit)), (:registry/required-technologies (vector :robotics :identity :audit-ledger)), (:actor/scope-excluded-ops (vector :finalize-guillotine-cutting-decision :authorize-binding-operation :proceed-with-finishing-binding-work :override-safety-officer-judgment :override-shop-safety-officer-judgment)), (:actor/robotics? true), (:adr/related (vector "2799007317-cloud-itonami-isco-7317-handicraft-workers-wood-basketry-coverage" "2799007315-cloud-itonami-isco-7315-glass-makers-cutters-grinders-coverage" "2799007314-cloud-itonami-isco-7314-potters-coverage" "2799007313-cloud-itonami-isco-7313-jewellery-precious-metal-workers-coverage" "2799007213-cloud-itonami-isco-7213-sheet-metal-workers-coverage")), (:adr/status :accepted), (:actor/scope-excluded-terms (vector "proceed with the guillotine-cutting operation" "proceed with the guillotine-cutting work" "proceed with the binding operation" "proceed with the folding operation" "finalize the guillotine-cutting decision" "finalize the binding decision" "authorize the binding operation" "authorize the guillotine-cutting operation" "override the shop safety officer's judgment" "override the safety officer's judgment" "override shop safety officer judgment" "override safety officer judgment")), (:adr/id 2799007323), (:phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:flag-safety-concern :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}}}"), (:actor/domain :manufacturing/print-finishing-binding-workshop-scheduling-coordination), (:actor/proposal-ops (vector :log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order)), (:actor/hard-checks (vector :worker-verified :workshop-verified :effect-propose :op-not-allowed :scope-exclusion)), (:registry/maturity :implemented), (:actor/isco-08 "7323"), (:actor/always-escalate-ops (vector :flag-safety-concern)), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:operation/nodes (vector :intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold)), (:operation/entry-point :intake), (:adr/body "# ADR 2799007323: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 7323 Print Finishing and Binding Workers workshop scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 7323\n-- Print Finishing and Binding Workers** only, Wave3 (production/\ntrades) of the rollout.\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"7323\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-\noccupation \\\"7323\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` sibling present at the correct `../technology` relative\npath), and its `:name` read exactly \"Print Finishing and Binding\nWorkers\" -- confirming the premise, no mismatch. Prior to this ADR the\nentry's `:maturity` was `:spec` with `:required-technologies\n[:robotics :identity :audit-ledger]` and no `:repo`/`:business-id`; no\nrepository existed at `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7323` (`gh\napi` 404 confirmed before scaffolding). This ADR and its companion\nregistry edit promote the `7323` entry to `:implemented`.\n\nPrint Finishing and Binding Workers operate cutting/folding/binding\nequipment on an active bindery floor -- real physical-safety stakes\n(blade/guillotine hazards, machine-pinch hazards). The controlling\nconstraint for this vertical is that the closed op allowlist must\nNEVER include any op that directly finalizes a finishing/binding-\nexecution decision (e.g. deciding to proceed with a specific\nguillotine-cutting, folding or binding operation), or overrides a\nshop safety officer's judgment -- those decisions must always be a\nhard permanent block or an always-escalate op, never auto-commit-\neligible. This actor is deliberately scoped to WORKSHOP SCHEDULING/\nLOGISTICS COORDINATION ONLY -- it never performs print-finishing/\nbinding work itself.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE and the\nclosed-allowlist + independently-verified-provenance safety pattern is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7213`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7213)\n(Sheet Metal Workers: `store`/`advisor`/`governor`/`actor` split,\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set, same Wave3 rollout, itself\ncarrying the physical-safety-domain shape forward from\n`cloud-itonami-isco-9311` Mining and Quarrying Labourers) -- cloned\nand read in full in this session. The blade/guillotine and\nmachine-pinch hazard vocabulary is new to this vertical (distinct from\n7213's cut/press-forming hazard vocabulary) but the closed allowlist +\nalways-escalate safety flag + content-based scope-exclusion with a\nself-trip regression test shape was mirrored closely, unchanged, from\nthat same reference.\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7323` as an OSS workshop\nscheduling/logistics-coordination actor for print finishing and\nbinding workers, following the SAME governed-actor architecture as\nevery prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this fleet: **Print\nFinishing and Binding Worker Advisor ⊣ PrintBindWorkerGovernor** on a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph (`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`,\ngit-sha-pinned identically to the reference's `deps.edn` -- a\ndifferent library coordinate from the `langgraph-clj` used by the\nunrelated `20-actors/*` actor family), with an independent Governor,\nhuman-in-the-loop approval via `interrupt-before`, and an append-only\naudit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **workshop scheduling/logistics\ncoordination ONLY, never direct finishing/binding-execution\nauthority** -- it must NEVER be designed to exercise, simulate\nexercising, or propose exercising a finishing/binding-execution\ndecision (e.g. a specific guillotine-cutting, folding or binding\noperation), or any override of a shop safety officer's judgment. These\nare not merely gated behind escalation -- they are structurally absent\nfrom the op-allowlist entirely.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- job/materials-usage/progress data logging\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/task/machine-time scheduling\n  proposal\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a blade-hazard/pinch-hazard/\n  equipment-condition concern, ALWAYS escalates, NEVER auto-commit\n  eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- binding-materials procurement\n  proposal\n\nThis actor has **NO op, anywhere in its allowlist, that resembles** a\nfinishing/binding-execution decision or a shop-safety-officer-\njudgment override. These are **structurally absent from the\nop-allowlist entirely**, not merely gated behind escalation -- an op\nsuch as `:finalize-guillotine-cutting-decision` cannot even be\nproposed by the reference mock advisor (its `infer`/`rationale-for`\nfunctions only ever emit one of the four allowlist ops), and if any\ncode path (a forged proposal, a future LLM advisor, a misbehaving\nfork) ever produced such an op, the governor's closed-allowlist HARD\ncheck (`:unknown-op`) rejects it unconditionally and permanently. A\nsecond, independent HARD check (`:scope-excluded-action`) names five\nconcretely-forbidden ops (`printbind.governor/scope-excluded-ops`:\n`:finalize-guillotine-cutting-decision`,\n`:authorize-binding-operation`,\n`:proceed-with-finishing-binding-work`,\n`:override-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`:override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`) as defense-in-depth, and is\nverified by dedicated unit tests\n(`printbind.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-guillotine-cutting-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-authorize-binding-operation`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-proceed-with-finishing-binding-work`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`).\n\n### Four HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Worker unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered worker record (`:no-worker`). Never\n   trusts the proposal's own claim of who the worker is.\n2. **Workshop unregistered** -- any proposal must cite an\n   independently registered workshop (`:no-workshop`). Together with\n   check 1, this directly implements the CRITICAL invariant that a\n   worker/shop record must be independently verified/registered\n   before any action.\n3. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (a claim to directly actuate outside governance)\n   (`:no-actuation`).\n4. **Op not allowed / scope-excluded action** -- any `:op` outside the\n   closed four-op allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`),\n   and independently, any proposal whose `:op` names one of the\n   concretely-forbidden ops above, OR whose free-text `:rationale`\n   names a finalization/execution action for proceeding with\n   guillotine-cutting, folding or binding work, or overriding a shop\n   safety officer's judgment, is a second HARD, PERMANENT block\n   (`:scope-excluded-action`), evaluated unconditionally on content --\n   defense-in-depth on top of the allowlist check: even if a future\n   change somehow widened the allowlist, content-based rejection still\n   independently blocks finishing/binding-execution/safety-override\n   language wherever it appears in free text.\n\n### One always-escalate (SOFT) gate, one threshold gate, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's implicit always-risky check). This is the\n  ONLY channel by which the robot may surface a blade-hazard/\n  guillotine-hazard/machine-pinch-hazard/equipment-condition\n  observation -- it never resolves the concern itself, and the\n  robot's role ends at \"here is the hazard data,\" never \"here is what\n  I recommend doing about shop safety.\"\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-cost-threshold` (2000, inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-threshold-boundary`) -- always needs human\n  sign-off, independent of confidence. This is an ESCALATION, not a\n  hard block, per the task's explicit domain design: an over-\n  threshold binding-materials order is not itself unsafe, unlike a\n  finishing/binding-execution or safety-officer-override attempt,\n  which is why it is handled by a different mechanism (soft escalate\n  vs. structural absence).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class, carried over from the sibling ISIC/ISCO tracks)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"cutting\", \"folding\", \"binding\", \"blade\") can accidentally match\ninside the mock advisor's own default rationale text for a legitimate\nproposal, self-blocking the actor's own happy path -- this is exactly\nthe risk this vertical's own vocabulary (a workshop coordination actor\nworking adjacent to guillotine-cutting/folding/binding work\nnecessarily discusses those concepts to do its scheduling/logging job)\ncould trigger if phrased carelessly. `printbind.governor/scope-\nexcluded-phrases` is phrased exclusively as finalization/execution\nACTIONS (e.g. \"proceed with the guillotine-cutting operation\",\n\"authorize the binding operation\", \"override the shop safety\nofficer's judgment\" -- matching the task's own worked example\nphrasing), never bare nouns, and `printbind.governor-\ntest/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-on-scope-exclusion`\nis a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed\nallowlist, driven through the default mock advisor, never trips\n`:scope-excluded-action`. The mock advisor's own default rationale\ntemplate was deliberately written to contain the bare nouns (\"logged\nwork record for worker ...\", \"scheduled crew operation for\nguillotine-cutting task ...\", \"... routed for shop safety officer\nreview\") WITHOUT containing any of the full finalization-action\nphrases, so the regression test is a genuine stress test of the\nbare-noun-vs-action-phrase distinction, not a vacuous pass. Green on\nfirst run in this session -- the scope-exclusion self-trip guard\nitself was never tripped during development.\n`printbind.actor-test/holds-a-scope-excluded-op-even-at-high-confidence`\nadditionally exercises the same invariant through the full graph run,\nconfirming a scope-excluded proposal never reaches `commit-record!`\nregardless of disposition path.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"7323\" ...}` entry\n  promoted from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id`\n  set to the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7323` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-7323`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately\n  before the edit).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 21 tests, 45 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's\n  `:test/counts` and in the task report, independently re-verified\n  against a brand-new fresh clone of the pushed repository (not just\n  the local working copy).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"Remove all .md, normalize ADRs to\n  tx-data\") -- a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string\n  blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-guillotine-cutting-decision`\n  or `:approve-binding-operation` that is merely gated behind an\n  always-escalate list: rejected outright per the task's explicit\n  domain-design guidance -- an always-escalate op still means the\n  *capability* to finalize a finishing/binding-execution decision\n  exists in the code path and is merely deferred to a human gate. For\n  a decision this severe (blade hazards, guillotine hazards,\n  machine-pinch hazards), the capability itself must not exist. The\n  only op related to shop-safety escalation is `:flag-safety-concern`,\n  which surfaces the need for human/shop-safety-officer attention and\n  never itself decides, authorizes, or defers a finishing/binding\n  decision for later automatic execution.\n- Making the supply-cost ceiling a HARD block (mirroring earlier\n  reference actors' transaction-amount-ceiling HARD checks): rejected\n  per the task's explicit domain design -- an over-threshold\n  binding-materials order is not itself unsafe, so it is handled as a\n  soft escalate gate, not a hard block; only the finishing/binding-\n  execution/safety-officer-override class is a hard, unconditional\n  block.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"cutting\" \"folding\"\n  \"binding\"]`): rejected outright per the fleet-known self-trip bug\n  class described above (and CLAUDE.md's own worked example for this\n  exact task), and per the explicit instruction to phrase\n  scope-exclusion terms as finalization/execution ACTIONS, never bare\n  nouns -- this actor's own domain necessarily discusses\n  cutting/folding/binding/safety-officer concepts to do its\n  scheduling/logging job, so a bare-noun list would risk self-\n  blocking the actor's own legitimate proposals (regression-tested\n  directly against rationale text that deliberately contains those\n  bare nouns).\n- Merging `worker` and `workshop` into a single entity (only checking\n  one provenance record): rejected -- the two-entity provenance shape\n  (independently-registered worker AND independently-registered\n  workshop) matches the CRITICAL invariant that a \"worker/shop record\n  must be independently verified/registered before any action\" and\n  the established pattern from prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actors\n  with two-sided provenance checks.\n\n## Itemized safety confirmation\n\nEvery op in this actor's closed proposal-op allowlist, and why it is\nsafe under the constraints above:\n\n1. **`:log-work-record`** -- job/materials-usage/progress data\n   logging only. Requires an independently registered worker AND\n   workshop (`:no-worker`/`:no-workshop`). Not a finishing/binding-\n   execution or safety-officer decision in any respect -- it is a\n   records-management action.\n2. **`:schedule-crew-operation`** -- crew/task/machine-time scheduling\n   proposal only. Cannot carry a finishing/binding-execution decision\n   (structurally absent from the op's field shape; any such attempt\n   via free text is caught by the `:scope-excluded-action` content\n   check). Does not authorize, finalize, or draw any conclusion about\n   a specific guillotine-cutting, folding or binding step -- it is a\n   calendar/logistics action.\n3. **`:flag-safety-concern`** -- surfaces a blade-hazard/guillotine-\n   hazard/machine-pinch-hazard/equipment-condition concern to a\n   human/shop safety officer; ALWAYS escalates, unconditionally, at\n   every confidence level, NEVER auto-commit eligible. This is the\n   ONLY channel through which a safety observation may be surfaced,\n   and it explicitly never resolves, decides, or acts on anything\n   itself -- the shop safety officer reviews and acts entirely on\n   their own authority.\n4. **`:coordinate-supply-order`** -- binding-materials procurement\n   proposal only (item, cost). Not a finishing/binding-execution or\n   authorization decision of any kind -- it is a purchasing-logistics\n   action, gated by ordinary cost-ceiling escalation (above 2000\n   always escalates).\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase, resembles\na finishing/binding-execution decision (e.g. proceeding with a\nspecific guillotine-cutting, folding or binding operation) or a\nshop-safety-officer-judgment override -- these categories are\nstructurally absent, not gated, confirmed by: (a) the closed four-op\nallowlist itself (`printbind.governor/allowed-ops`), (b) five\nconcretely-named forbidden-op fixtures rejected at the governor-unit\nlevel (`printbind.governor/scope-excluded-ops`,\n`printbind.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-guillotine-cutting-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-authorize-binding-operation`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-proceed-with-finishing-binding-work`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`),\nand (c) a content-based scope-exclusion check independent of the\n`:op` field (`printbind.governor/scope-excluded-phrases`,\n`.../contains-excluded-phrase?`), tested directly against a rationale\nthat attempts to proceed with guillotine-cutting work or override a\nshop safety officer's judgment even via an otherwise-allowlisted op\n(`printbind.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-even-with-allowlisted-op`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-override-shop-safety-officer`).\n"), (:adr/date "2026-07-18"), (:actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order 2000}"), (:test/counts "{:total 21, :assertions 45, :failures 0, :errors 0}"), (:actor/coordination? true), (:actor/name "Print Finishing and Binding Workshop Scheduling Coordination Practice"), (:db/id -1), (:test/coverage (vector :governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :worker-verification :workshop-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-cost-threshold-escalation)), (:registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-7323"), (:registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7323"), (:adr/scope (vector :kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7323)), (:test/simulator :printbind.actor-test), (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-7323 — Print Finishing and Binding Workers Workshop Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage"), (:adr/source-format "edn"), (:adr/references (vector 2607121000)), (:actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-7323)))
